mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Lutix DeepTech Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis canister backs the Lutix DeepTech company website. Its only product feature is the public contact/enquiry form: a visitor submits their name, email, optional company and message, the enquiry is stored durably, and the Lutix DeepTech team is notified by email. An admin-only read endpoint lists stored enquiries.\n\n## Public methods\n\n### `submitEnquiry(input : EnquiryInput) : async SubmitResult`\n\nStores a new enquiry and emails the team. `EnquiryInput` is `{ name : Text; email : Text; company : ?Text; message : Text }`.\n\n- **Authentication:** none required. Anonymous callers are allowed; this is the public website form.\n- **Authorization:** none. Any caller may submit.\n- **Validation:** `name`, `email` and `message` must be non-empty. A blank required field returns `#err(\"Name, email and message are required.\")` and stores nothing.\n- **Returns:** `#ok(id)` with the assigned `EnquiryId` (`Nat`) on success, or `#err(text)` with a human-readable message on validation failure.\n- **Side effects:** the enquiry is persisted, then a notification email is sent to the team. The email send is best-effort: a failed send does not roll back the stored enquiry and does not change the returned result.\n- **Retry safety:** NOT idempotent. Each successful call creates a new enquiry with a new id and sends another email. Do not auto-retry a submission that may have succeeded; a retry duplicates the record and the notification.\n\n### `listEnquiries() : async [Enquiry]`\n\nReturns every stored enquiry, newest first (descending `id`).\n\n- **Authentication:** a signed (non-anonymous) caller is required in practice, because the authorization check below rejects anonymous principals.\n- **Authorization:** admin only. A non-admin caller traps with `Unauthorized: Only admins can list enquiries`.\n- **Returns:** an array of `Enquiry` records: `{ id : EnquiryId; name : Text; email : Text; company : ?Text; message : Text; submittedAt : Timestamp }`.\n- **Read-only:** declared `query`; it never mutates state.\n\n### `getApiDoc() : async Text`\n\nReturns this document. Public query, no authentication.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nThe app uses Internet Identity through the platform authorization mixin. The first authenticated principal to sign in becomes the admin; subsequent sign-ins are ordinary users. `listEnquiries` is guarded by `isAdmin`, so only that admin principal (or any principal later assigned the admin role) can read the enquiry list.\n\nThe frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that already holds the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nRegistration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend. A principal that never did so is unregistered even if it belongs to the app owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered. An unregistered or anonymous caller calling `listEnquiries` receives the trap `Unauthorized: Only admins can list enquiries`.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- `Timestamp` is a signed `Int` count of nanoseconds since the Unix epoch, produced by `Time.now()`. It is not milliseconds or seconds.\n- `EnquiryId` is a `Nat` assigned monotonically by the backend, starting at 0.\n- `company` is optional (`?Text`); absent means the visitor left it blank.\n- `SubmitResult` is a variant: `#ok(EnquiryId)` or `#err(Text)`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n`submitEnquiry` completes in a single call: it stores the enquiry and awaits the email send before returning. There is no job to poll. `listEnquiries` is a query and reflects committed state immediately.\n\n## Errors and limits\n\n- Validation failure returns `#err(text)`; it is not a trap, so the caller can display the message.\n- Authorization failure on `listEnquiries` traps and rolls back the call.\n- The email notification is sent to a fixed internal team address; callers cannot choose the recipient.\n- There is no pagination on `listEnquiries`; it returns the full set.\n";
  };
};
